<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="24.2" level="1">Elections</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="5" level="2">Candidates for Office</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="4" level="3">Conduct of Primaries</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>24.2-519</section_number>
	<catch_line>Qualification of primary candidates</catch_line>
	<text>
		In order to qualify as a candidate at any primary, a person must be legally qualified to hold the office for which he is a candidate and be qualified to vote in the primary in which he seeks to be a candidate.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 24-369; 1970, c. 462, § 24.1-183; 1971, Ex. Sess., c. 226; 1974, c. 428; 1977, c. 490; 1993, c. 641.</history>
</law>
